message: "If you use this dataset, code, or any of the numbers in this report, cite it as below."
title: "China's Sports Lottery is not a betting market - it's a formula"
abstract: >-
  897 Chinese Sports Lottery (竞彩) football matches, 2026-05-17 to 2026-09-25, each paired with the
  same fixture's European "99 bookmakers average" closing odds. The lottery carries a 12.92% margin
  with sigma = 0.0006; the European average carries 6.85% with sigma = 0.0109. The lottery is more
  expensive in 897 of 897 matches. The finding is that the lottery's price barely moves because it is
  computed from a fixed payout parameter rather than set by a market: a price that does not move
  cannot be wrong, so there is no mispricing to find. Also includes 15 betting rules over a
  1,617-bet sample, none of which passes a pre-registered threshold of n >= 300 and 95% CI lower
  bound > 0.
